629,"_gp_fcf_yield":true,"_score_fcf_yield":76.4,"_gate_int_coverage":4.273986690865094,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":17.2,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":0.17554433917236004,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":85.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.018621138366700728,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":11.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.3188791870197366,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":23.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.3627624682566974,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":0.008316631012689715,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":4.2,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.05293917316469085,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":51.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.03286102713211059,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":41.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.017870968294478522,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":32.1,"_gate_fund_growth":0.0398897559430694,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":39.9,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02628916713257187,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":40.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03753544029344247,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":3.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010706054024805105,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":82.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.016970001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":11.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Tidewater Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides offshore support vessels and marine support services to the offshore energy industry through the operation of a fleet of offshore marine service vessels worldwide. The company operates through five segments: Americas, Asia Pacific, Middle East, Europe/Mediterranean, and West Africa. It offers phases of offshore crude oil and natural gas exploration, field development, production, maintenance, and windfarm development and maintenance activities; towing and anchor handling for mobile offshore drilling units; transportation of supplies and personnel necessary to sustain drilling, workover, and production operations; and field abandonment, dismantlement, and restoration activities. The company also provides offshore construction; seismic and subsea support; various other specialized services, such as pipe laying, cable laying, and geotechnical survey support for windfarm construction. Its vessels consist of anchor handling towing supply vessels, platform supply vessels, and other specialty vessels, as well as crew boats, utility vessels, and offshore tugs. The company serves integrated and independent oil and gas exploration, development, and production companies; mid-sized and smaller independent exploration and production companies; foreign government-owned or government-controlled organizations engaged in the exploration, development, and production of oil and gas; offshore drilling contractors; and other companies that provide services to the offshore energy industry comprising offshore construction companies, windfarm development companies, diving companies, and well stimulation companies. Tidewater Inc. was incorporated in 1956 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Quintin V. Kneen CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $185K ranks in the bottom quartile among Energy peers. Each employee generates $48K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Tidewater Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.4B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 1% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $353M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.13\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries a 41% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.40646119569253614},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Energy peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Financial quality scores above most Energy peers","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (TDW) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/17/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_TDW_Edition_111926125401_1795110841.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795110841.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tidewater (NYSE:TDW) Rating Lowered to Strong Sell at Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/tidewater-nysetdw-rating-lowered-to-strong-sell-at-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794771068.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.751,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Does Tighter Revenue Guidance Change The Bull Case For Tidewater Stock (TDW)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-tdw/tidewater/news/does-tighter-revenue-guidance-change-the-bull-case-for-tidew","date"